    desc: 'Tingatinga began when Tanzanian painter Edward Saidi Tingatinga painted small vivid panels in Dar es Salaam from 1968, working on masonite with several layers of bicycle paint that give brilliant, highly saturated color. The images are naive and caricatural, with humor and sarcasm often explicit; subjects — the Big Five and other wildlife, village life, invented spirits — were sized small and shaped square for the tourist market, leading some to call them "airport paintings". Spread by followers and the Tingatinga Arts Cooperative Society, the genre became the most widely represented painting style of Tanzania and Kenya, even inspiring the Tinga Tinga Tales animation.',
